WEBVTT

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.130
"February 28th - 6:05 PM"

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.010
"February 28th - 6:05 PM"
What a bad planner.
So much for my farewell party.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.470
"Jazz Bar 'Zvezda'"
What a bad planner.
So much for my farewell party.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:18.470
Sorry.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.430
"Closed"

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.520
Hold up. I thought today was
to wish me luck, not your farewell par--

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:33.190
Quit your yapping. Wishing you luck...
might've been part of it.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.030
Oh, well. Let's try somewhere else.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.030
Mmm.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:58.390
"Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut"

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:12.840
"A Cold Spring"

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:20.010
"Movie Theater"
What's this? Hey! When?! Who?!
They're on the moon?! It can't be real!

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.050
"The Heavenly Voyage"
--It's not real.
--Huh? It's not?

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.100
"To the moon! Carry the dreams
of humanity into the darkness of space!"
It's just a movie.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.640
"To the moon! Carry the dreams
of humanity into the darkness of space!"
Movie?

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.100
--Wanna watch it?
--Mmm!

00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:00.010
Awesome! Is that real?! Look, it's flying!

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.430
Yeah.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.600
Awesome!

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.100
Wh-Whoa! Look out! Ack!

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.940
Ahh, look what you did.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.570
Sorry.

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.400
No problem. We'll clean it later.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.610
Let's not miss the movie.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:22.780
Mmm.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.010
--Well done!
--Hey, sit down!

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.430
Huh? Oh.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.260
Thank goodness! What a relief!

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.320
I'm getting hungry.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.240
Wanna get something?

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:11.160
No, look!

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:16.670
Anya said to bring this.
It's dinner... for two.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:17.920
Hmm?

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:26.890
Great. Then let's go somewhere
with a view. It's a night picnic.

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.010
Mmm!

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.720
"Belka Lake"

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.060
What's this?

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.650
Open and see.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.740
Whoa, is that <i>kholodets</i>?!

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.450
Did you make this?

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:55.210
Anya said it's food
for celebrations in the UZSR.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.830
A celebration? For what?

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:06.260
A pre-celebration! 'Cuz if you get picked
to fly, I probably won't be around.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:11.100
I'll cut it for you, so have some.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.220
Sure.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:19.020
--Here.
--Yeah, thanks.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:30.080
Well?

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.410
It's good. It's really good!

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:40.460
Thank goodness! I was worried
'cuz I can't taste it.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:43.920
Speaking of which,
how'd you nail the flavor?

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:47.220
I had Anya be my taste tester.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.560
That must've been rough.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:01.440
Hey, since you ate that, you better
get picked as the first cosmonaut.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:05.530
Of course. Otherwise,
you'll turn me into a mummy.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:26.880
I saw the aurora from space, too.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.890
It looked like a curtain over the globe.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.930
So pretty.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.600
Mmm.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:07.800
I want her to suck my blood.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:15.310
I want to feel that sweet pain once more.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:23.100
I can't make sense of why,
but my instincts want it.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:27.150
Not in my arm, but with a bite in my neck.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.580
Irina.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.080
It's not weird.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.580
Mmm.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:50.720
Irina, go ahead.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.300
Right.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.160
What's wrong?

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.330
--The bus is coming.
--Huh?

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:27.420
You don't want to be seen with me, right?

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:31.970
Sorry.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:37.720
That's not true.
You've done nothing wrong.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.100
But--

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:41.140
Say nothing more.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.350
Lev...

00:08:54.950 --> 00:09:00.540
No. Don't worry about me. Do your best.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:04.960
When you get back from space,
we'll meet again.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:11.920
It's a promise.

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:23.810
Lev? Why are you way out here?

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:26.850
A picnic.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.150
Huh?

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.030
"March 1st - 8:15 PM"
Are you ready to go, Irinyan?

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:36.490
"Biomedical Laboratory"
Are you ready to go, Irinyan?

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:37.660
"Biomedical Laboratory"
Yeah.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:58.970
"The First Human Spaceflight in History"

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.390
"April 4th - 10:03 AM"

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:02.260
"April 4th - 10:03 AM"
I spoke with the capital a moment ago.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.850
"Training Center - Lecture Hall"
I spoke with the capital a moment ago.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:05.270
"Training Center - Lecture Hall"
The flight will occur sometime
between April 10th and 20th.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:17.280
In the earliest case, that gives us
less than one week to go.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:23.160
I'm sure you're all anxious to know
which cosmonaut it will be.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:29.120
A special committee at Albinar
is supposed to make the decision,

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:31.790
but we don't know exactly when.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.920
Understood.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:40.180
At 5 o'clock today, we'll leave
the city to prepare for the launch.

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:42.600
--Go get ready!
--Yes, sir!

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:52.940
"April 5th - 0:35 PM"
After leaving Laika44, the bus headed
not for the Albinar Cosmodrome,

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:54.480
"Sangrad - Glorious Square"
After leaving Laika44, the bus headed
not for the Albinar Cosmodrome,

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.940
"Sangrad - Glorious Square"
but for the Founder's
Mausoleum in Sangrad.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:06.580
That is, to preserve on film a record
of the first human spaceflight.

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:11.750
However, the only ones being
filmed were Lev and Mikhail.

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:18.010
In other words, the decision had
been narrowed down to those two.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.880
You two look far too tense.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.090
Huh?

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:28.730
Though, if you're paying respect to
the Founder, I suppose a stern look works.

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:34.190
It's supposed to be a glimpse into
your daily lives. Try to look happy.

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:35.570
You're...!

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.530
Yes. Long time no see.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.860
Comrade Secretary.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:41.030
What are you doing here?

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:45.780
Isn't it obvious? This seemed interesting.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:50.000
Um, you said we're
filming our daily lives?

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.790
Yes, I did.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:53.880
Except, this is Sangrad.

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.920
Indeed. What that means is...

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:03.590
Since before and after the launch,
this has been your home.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:10.930
I see. The public can never know
about the closed city, Laika44.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:25.620
Great, good job! Let's take a break.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:30.750
It's pretty tiring to act out daily life.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.580
It sure is.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:36.920
Watching people get filmed
is surprisingly boring.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:44.090
I think I'll get going, but first,
let me share something with you.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:51.560
If the flight is a success,
we'll be holding a ceremony here.

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:57.940
Some 200,000 people will gather for the
largest celebration since our founding.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:03.490
As far as the eye can see--
people, people, people.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:08.700
Their 400,000 eyes staring at a hero.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:16.710
Knowing that, what kind of person
should the first human in space be?

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:19.750
Someone suited to be a great hero.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:24.720
Mmm. That's correct. And Lev?

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.890
The most suitable person is me.

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:31.970
...is what I want to say,
but I don't know.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:33.730
How honest.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:37.520
But I know what they'll
need more than anything.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:38.770
Hmm?

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:43.230
The yearning to fly in space,
even if it costs their life.

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:51.830
That's also correct.
Thanks for your answers. Goodbye.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.790
Um...!

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.370
What is it?

00:13:55.370 --> 00:14:02.300
For reference, what kind of person
do you think a cosmonaut should be?

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.170
H-Hey...

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:09.680
Let's see... A revolutionary who
will lead us to the new world.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:17.810
Or something. Let's meet again
when you get back from space.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.980
Well, safe travels.

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:27.860
Hey, do you think everything
she said was a lie?

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.490
Yeah, maybe.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:42.590
They're selling ice cream, Irinyan!

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:47.050
Hey, Anya. Could you stop
calling me Irinyan?

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.340
Huh? Why's that?

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:52.800
Because you're older than me.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.390
Hmm.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:58.100
Well, how about Irina-<i>chan</i>?

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:01.520
--Chan?
--Is that bad?

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:02.980
Suit yourself.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:04.770
Okay, I will!

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:09.530
I'll get ice cream,
so wait right here, Irina!

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:10.990
Mmm.

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:13.530
Jeez, that Anya...

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:20.870
That's...!

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:28.260
Lev...

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:31.050
Lev...!

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:33.680
Lev!

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:42.560
Where are you going?

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.560
Irin--!

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.150
Keep an eye on her!

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:51.780
My apologies.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:55.450
Irina!

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.830
Don't run off on your own.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.840
"Sangrad -
National Military Medical Center"

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:24.440
Open your mouth.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:31.400
I'm transferring--I'll be working
at the Design Bureau.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:35.200
Of course I'm not working
at the Design Bureau.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:38.120
I wonder if he still believes it.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:43.290
Though I am undergoing exams,
so half of it is true.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:48.000
But that'll stop when
a human goes to space.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:53.930
After the flight, my existence
is nothing but a nuisance.

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:55.720
I'll probably be...

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:09.940
Good job with the exams, Irina.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:12.400
Hey, who was with Lev today?

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:15.070
That was Mikhail.

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:18.780
Then, if those cameras
were filming them...

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:22.870
One of them will be picked
as the cosmonaut!

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:24.000
I knew it.

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:31.170
It's incredible! Lev is just one
step away from fulfilling his dream!

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:32.760
Yeah.

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:44.770
All right. Let's make him
our motherland's hero.

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:47.980
Very well. Also...

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:53.110
The Delivery Crew has done
enough follow-up exams for N44.

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:55.900
They want to dispose of her.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:59.030
Is there value in keeping her around?

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:04.910
She's too cute to simply kill.
Sell her as an actress or singer.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.290
"Dhampir = Half Vampire"
The UK has a dhampir star or two.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.090
"Dhampir = Half Vampire"
You're kidding, right?

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:19.930
I'm kidding, but it's true that I welcome
a revolution of this boring world.

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:26.100
A revolution that consumes both
the UK and the Delivery Crew in one go.

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:30.110
Don't you as well?

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:35.360
The vampire, Irina Luminesk...

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:38.950
Couldn't she be a weapon for that purpose?

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:42.330
"April 6th - 5:08 AM"

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:46.330
"April 9th - 11:46 AM"

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.080
"Albinar Cosmodrome - Staff Dormitory"

00:18:54.460 --> 00:19:01.640
The launch will be in three days,
on April 12th at 9 in the morning.

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:09.140
As for who's flying...

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:12.480
Private Lev Leps, it's you.

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:13.650
Huh?

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:16.280
Sir!

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:22.570
Why?! I've done better
than him in every field!

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:25.290
Why was Lev chosen?!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:30.500
Our motherland's rocket flies
with everyone's dreams.

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:35.960
Only someone who can make
people smile and carry their dreams

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:38.880
is fit to be our hero.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:41.760
That was the basis for choosing?

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:45.390
No, that's my personal opinion.

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:49.640
Private Mikhail.

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:54.150
If Lev is unable to, you will fly instead.

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:56.820
Be prepared to do so.

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:57.980
Yes, sir.

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:02.360
"Albinar Cosmodrome - Rocket Hangar"

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:04.410
Whoa!

00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:08.450
It's been a while.

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:10.160
It has, Chief.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:13.580
How are you doing? You've lost weight.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:18.130
I feel great, now that
I've seen your face again.

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:19.880
My call sign?

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:27.390
Yeah. I wanted to pick one with you
now that you're going to space.

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:31.140
How did you come up
with Irina's "Lycoris"?

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:36.150
That? The meaning of lycoris as a flower.

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:39.690
It's, "I hope we meet again soon."

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:41.360
Did you tell her?

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:48.580
I did. She was glad to know it meant
I hoped she came back safe.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.750
I see.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:58.040
Well, is there a flower for praying
that someone far away stays safe?

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:01.800
I want to wish someone that from space.

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:08.510
There is! Aster!

00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:09.930
Aster...

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:14.640
"Sangrad -
National Military Medical Center"

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.130
Irina.

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:42.460
Lev?

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:45.840
It's time, Irina.

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:50.350
Mmm.

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.010
"Next Episode:
'Lies and Truths'"
